From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:41:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Restructure to the team code convention; add serving,
 notebooks, packaging

Layout: configs/{train,deploy}/*.yaml, data/{raw,processed,samples},
docs/{design,experiment_log,api_spec}.md, notebooks/{eda,poc_model}.ipynb,
src/{data,features,models,evaluation,serving,utils}, tests/test_{data_loader,model,serving}.py,
scripts/{train,eval,serve,extract_features}.sh, requirements.txt, setup.py, Dockerfile.

- One trainer (src/models/trainer.py) and one evaluator (src/evaluation/evaluate.py)
  for image and multimodal heads, chosen by the config's task key.
- Feature caches move to data/processed/features/; recorded features/<name> paths
  resolve both ways, so shipped heads, old run configs and archives unpacked at the
  repository root keep working.
- Serving: MultimodalPredictor (training preprocessing, trained fusion head) and a
  FastAPI app with /health, /model, /predict, /predict/batch; uploads are checked
  for size, format, pixel count and aspect ratio before decoding.
- Behaviour unchanged: retraining and replays are byte-identical to the old code
  (docs/Multimodal_Test_Results.md, 2026-10-17). 54 tests (1 skipped without PowerShell).

